{"name":"Natural Youth","hex":"#d7e5b4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.","Normally associated with a particular person or thing; inherently related to the nature of a thing or creature."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"youth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality or state of being young.","The part of life following childhood; the period of existence preceding maturity or age; the whole early part of life, from childhood, or, sometimes, from infancy, to adulthood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Youth","blocks":[{"text":"Youth is the time of life when one is young. The word, youth, can also mean the time between childhood and adulthood (maturity), but it can also refer to one's peak, in terms of health or the period of life known as being a young adult. Youth is also defined as \"the appearance, freshness, vigor, spirit, etc., characteristic of one, who is young\". Its definitions of a specific age range varies, as youth is not defined chronologically as a stage that can be tied to specific age ranges; nor can its end point be linked to specific activities, such as taking unpaid work, or having sexual relations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/1970sgirls.jpg/330px-1970sgirls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Youth","wikidata":"Q190007"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/1970sgirls.jpg/500px-1970sgirls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/1970sgirls.jpg/5